NAME: a variable next to a plain reference
DESCRIPTION: (MOV x (Dir -1)) with x in the A-field moves x's value into the plain reference's B-field (MOV.AB): beside a value, a cell is its B-field; see behtests/mixed_operand_field.beh
SRC:
(let (x 7)
  (seq
    (JMP (Dir 3))
    (DAT (store x) 0)
    (DAT 0 0)
    (MOV x (Dir -1))
    (JMP 0) ))
EXPECTED:
;redcode-94b

  JMP    $3     , #0     
_LET1 
  DAT    #7     , #0     
  DAT    #0     , #0     
  MOV.AB $_LET1 , $-1    
  JMP    #0     , #0     
  DAT    $0     , $0     